<x-legal-layout title="Privacy policy" description="How CityCare Medical Centre uses and safeguards patient, clinical, account and payment information.">
    <section id="responsibility">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-950">1. Who is responsible for your information</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">CityCare Medical Centre in Kampala, Uganda manages the information used in its website, patient portal and clinic workflows. This policy explains what information is handled, why it is used and how you can ask about it.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="information">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-950">2. Information used by CityCare</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">Depending on the services you use, CityCare may handle:</p>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1.5 ps-5">
            <li><strong>Identity and contact details:</strong> name, patient number, date of birth, phone, email, address and emergency contact information.</li>
            <li><strong>Care information:</strong> appointments, symptoms, diagnoses, treatment notes, allergies, prescriptions, laboratory orders and results, and visit history.</li>
            <li><strong>Account and security information:</strong> account identifiers, password hashes, sign-in and verification events, role and access records, and audit events.</li>
            <li><strong>Billing information:</strong> fees, amounts paid, balances, payment method, receipt references and transaction status. Online payment card or mobile money credentials are entered with the payment provider rather than stored as account fields in the CityCare portal.</li>
            <li><strong>Technical information:</strong> session and essential cookie data, request and error logs, and basic device or connection information needed to operate and protect the service.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="purposes">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-950">3. Why information is used</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">CityCare uses information to create and manage patient accounts; arrange consultations and tests; support clinical care and follow-up; manage prescriptions and medicine stock; prepare bills and receipts; process payments; communicate about accounts and visits; protect the service; and meet applicable operational and legal requirements.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="access-sharing">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-950">4. Who may receive or access information</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">Access within CityCare is assigned by role and job responsibility. Reception, clinicians, laboratory staff, pharmacists and cashiers can access the parts needed for their duties. Patients can access their own portal information after sign-in.</p>
        <p class="mt-2">CityCare may use service providers that support hosting, account messages, technical operations and online payments. PesaPal processes the hosted online checkout and returns transaction details to CityCare. Providers receive information needed to perform their service. Information may also be disclosed where required by applicable law or necessary to protect a person’s safety, the clinic or the service.</p>
        <p class="mt-2">CityCare does not offer patient records for sale or use them for advertising profiles.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="safeguards">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-950">5. Safeguards and retention</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">CityCare uses account authentication, role-based permissions, password hashing and access records to help protect information. No online service can guarantee that every transmission or system will be uninterrupted or free from risk; report suspected account or privacy issues to clinic administration promptly.</p>
        <p class="mt-2">Clinical and billing records are kept for care continuity, accounting, operational and legal purposes under the clinic’s retention practices. Where an account is deactivated, related clinical records may remain linked to past visits so that those records are not lost. Access and use remain subject to applicable privacy obligations.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="cookies">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-950">6. Cookies and online checkout</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">The portal uses essential session and security cookies to keep users signed in and protect forms. The site does not use advertising cookies for targeted ads. When you choose online payment, you leave the portal for the payment provider’s checkout and that provider’s privacy terms also apply during checkout.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="your-choices">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-950">7. Your choices and privacy requests</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">You may ask CityCare to explain the information associated with your account, request access to or correction of inaccurate details, or raise a concern about how information is used. Requests can be made to CityCare reception or clinic administration in Kampala. CityCare may need to verify your identity and may retain or use some clinical or transaction records where required for care, accounting or legal purposes.</p>
        <p class="mt-2">For information about Uganda’s data protection framework or to raise a concern with the national oversight office, visit the <a href="https://pdpo.go.ug/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="font-semibold text-teal-800 underline">Personal Data Protection Office of Uganda</a>. The <a href="https://ulii.org/en/akn/ug/act/2019/9/eng%402023-12-31" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="font-semibold text-teal-800 underline">Data Protection and Privacy Act</a> is available through the Uganda Legal Information Institute.</p>
    </section>

    <section id="policy-changes">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-950">8. Updates and questions</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">CityCare may update this policy as services or information practices change. The latest version and update date will be published here. For a privacy question or request, speak with CityCare reception or clinic administration.</p>
        <p class="mt-3">Also read the <a href="{{ route('legal.terms') }}" class="font-semibold text-teal-800 underline">Terms of use</a>.</p>
    </section>
</x-legal-layout>
